  "verified_against": {
    "source": "release-manifest.json",
    "agrees": true,
    "note": "Hashes were downloaded from the published v5.41.0 release assets and hashed independently, then checked again by re-fetching the URL this pin itself names. Only the pegasus artifact changed: install.sh and the two builder scripts are byte-identical to v5.28.0 and earlier. v5.41.0 reaches this distribution through the rendered permission of every agent it embarks, so it changes what each of them may touch under DARQ's own names. OpenCode does not render a permission prompt raised by a sub-agent two levels down: the view that lists pending requests walks a single level of the session tree and returns nothing at all once the session it is showing has a parent, so the ask never reaches a screen and the tool call waits forever, with no timeout to end it (anomalyco/opencode#39112, open, with #43996 and #44747 beside it and a #30635 that was closed having fixed only one level). This distribution embarks subagent_depth 10, so two levels is the ordinary shape of a delegation here, not an exotic one -- which is why the hang was reached on an ordinary run. The external_directory baseline therefore moves from ask to allow, so that nothing this distribution embarks can raise a prompt nobody would ever see. It is a workaround with a named end: the day the upstream view walks the whole tree, the baseline returns to ask, and the engine's own docstring says so in the place where the revert would be written. What stays denied is a small fixed floor -- .ssh/, .aws/, .credentials/, .config/gh/, secrets/ -- written after every grant so the runtime's last-match resolution lands on it. That floor denies the canonical spelling of those five directories and nothing more: matching is textual, the runtime never resolves a path, and an agent holding the shell under an open baseline can build the indirection itself. It is a guard against an agent that wanders in, not a boundary against one that means to arrive, and both the manual and the architecture row now say exactly that rather than claiming it always denies. A directory granted through the distribution's own grant command is dormant under this baseline rather than pointless: it is still recorded and regains its full meaning the day the baseline returns. This distribution changed nothing of its own for this pin beyond the alignment."
  }
}
